  "query_preview": "..Satellite imagery this morning showed a upper\nlevel trof moving through the intermountain west with srn AZ on\nthe tail end of this system. Will see high clouds pass through\ntoday with high temperatures at or slightly cooler than Sunday.\nOvernight lows into Tuesday morning will once again be on the \nchilly to cold side with isolated freezing areas again for the \nvalleys east of Tucson that say a freeze yesterday morning.\nProgressive pattern continues with high pressure over the area\non Tuesday, bringing warmer high temperatures. Another trof\nmoves through Wednesday then high pressure strengthens over the\narea Thanksgiving Day into the upcoming weekend bringing warmer\nhigh temperatures with readings in the upper 70s to lower 80s\nthis weekend. Pattern change next week bring the prospects for \nprecipitation returning to the region, but there is uncertainty\nin the ensembles.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (Mon Nov 30 to Sat Dec 5)\nTemperature: Near normal\nPrecipitation: Leaning above normal (43%-45%)",
